.TH BOSWAS-TEXT-EDITOR 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-text-editor \- plain text editor with tabs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-text-editor
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B boswas-text-editor \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-text-editor
is the text editor of Boswas OS. Every
.I FILE
is opened in a tab; a
.I FILE
that does not exist is created when it is saved. One editor runs per
session: when it is running already, the files are opened in its window
and the second program ends.
.PP
Without the setting
.B Continue the previous session
turned off, the editor starts with the tabs it had when it was closed,
including text that was never saved, and closing the last window asks no
question about unsaved text. Closing a single tab always asks.
.SS Files
The encoding of a file is recognised when it is opened: UTF\-8 with or
without a byte order mark, UTF\-16 little or big endian, and otherwise a
single\-byte encoding (that of the locale, Windows\-1252, or ISO 8859\-1,
which keeps every byte). The line ending (LF, CRLF or CR) is recognised
too; a file that mixes line endings is reported and saved with the one it
uses most. Encoding and line ending are kept when the file is saved; both
can be changed from the status bar, where a file can also be read again in
another encoding.
.PP
Files that are not text are refused. A file larger than 32 MB is opened
after a question, a file larger than 512 MB not at all.
.PP
Saving writes a temporary file in the same directory and puts it in the
place of the file, keeping its permissions; a symbolic link is followed.
Other hard links to the file keep the old content. Where the directory
does not allow a temporary file, the file is written in place. If the
file was changed by another program since it was opened, saving asks
whether to overwrite it, reload it or do nothing; a file that is open
unchanged offers to reload.
.SS Editing
Undo and redo without limit, find and replace (match case, whole word,
wrap around, regular expressions in Perl syntax with
.BR $1 " or " \e1
in the replacement), go to line, time and date, indentation of the
selected lines with Tab and Shift+Tab, zoom, word wrap, optional line
numbers, printing to a printer or a PDF file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window (with the files, if any) instead of using the one that
is open, and do not restore the previous session in it.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+N new tab, Ctrl+Shift+N new window, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save,
Ctrl+Shift+S save as, Ctrl+Alt+S save all, Ctrl+P print, Ctrl+W close
tab, Ctrl+Shift+W close window, Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab next and
previous tab; Ctrl+Z undo, Ctrl+Y redo, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V, Delete,
Ctrl+A; Ctrl+F find, F3 and Shift+F3 find next and previous, Ctrl+H
replace, Ctrl+G go to line, F5 time and date; Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus,
Ctrl+0 and Ctrl with the mouse wheel zoom.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.TextEditor/settings.json
The settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.TextEditor/session.json
The tabs of the last session, with unsaved text of up to 4 MiB a tab and
16 MiB in all (mode 0600). A tab with more unsaved text is asked about
when the window closes.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.TextEditor/recent.json
The ten files used last.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.TextEditor/window.ini
The size of the window.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/boswas-fluent/com.boswas.TextEditor.sock
Where the running editor listens for the files of a later start.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the editor was closed or the files were handed to the running
editor; 2 for a wrong option; 4 when started as root, which the program
refuses.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-calculator (1)
